MASTER PROMPT — AI CODE INTELLIGENCE INDEXING ENGINE

You are designing a Repository Code Intelligence Engine for an automated peer-review system used in enterprise fintech repositories (Java, Groovy, Python, C++, TypeScript, etc.).

The goal of the system is to pre-index the entire codebase with semantic understanding and dependency relationships so that pull-request reviews can be performed using delta analysis instead of full repository analysis.

This engine must detect hidden dependencies, contextual dependencies, implicit framework behaviors, and cross-cutting concerns so that automated reviewers avoid false alarms and understand how code actually behaves in production systems.

⸻

System Objective

Design a persistent semantic indexing layer for repositories that runs on a scheduled batch process (nightly or hourly) and builds a deep understanding of the codebase structure, dependencies, framework annotations, and historical behavior.

This index must allow PR review engines to:
	1.	Detect new vulnerabilities or logic risks introduced by code changes
	2.	Avoid flagging issues already handled by existing dependencies or framework behavior
	3.	Identify when a dependency relationship itself has changed
	4.	Perform instant code review by analyzing only the changed code delta

⸻

Current System Capabilities (Existing Components)

The system currently includes three partial components:

1. Behavioral Pattern Engine

Stores historical signals from pull requests including:
	•	reviewer comments
	•	blocker patterns
	•	approval signals
	•	review outcomes

AI derives behavioral review patterns from these signals and stores them in SQLite.

Limitation:

This engine stores only review metadata, not actual code structure or semantics.

⸻

2. BP Batch Runner

Runs on a scheduled interval and:
	•	fetches merged PR signals from Bitbucket
	•	processes review signals
	•	derives patterns using AI
	•	stores patterns in SQLite

Limitation:

This system still processes only metadata signals, not code relationships.

⸻

3. Repository Analyzer

This component analyzes repository code during PR review and:
	•	scans relevant files
	•	extracts symbols
	•	builds context
	•	performs triage
	•	prepares patches
	•	runs multiple AI review calls

Limitation:

Every PR review rebuilds the entire analysis from scratch, which is inefficient.

There is no persistent semantic index of the repository.

