Core Concept

The repository indexing system must build a semantic dependency graph including:
	•	code structure
	•	method relationships
	•	framework annotations
	•	dependency injection
	•	configuration-driven behavior
	•	database relationships
	•	service communication patterns

This graph becomes the source of truth for code understanding.

⸻

Key Dependency Types to Detect

The engine must detect and index the following dependency categories.

Hidden Dependencies

Dependencies not visible in local code but influencing behavior.

Examples:
	•	annotations
	•	dependency injection
	•	AOP interceptors
	•	configuration files
	•	framework wiring

⸻

Context Dependencies

Code correctness depends on behavior defined elsewhere.

Examples:
	•	validation performed upstream
	•	authorization middleware
	•	transaction boundaries
	•	sanitization layers

⸻

Implicit Dependencies

Dependencies introduced by frameworks or runtime environments.

Examples:
	•	Spring dependency injection
	•	Lombok generated methods
	•	ORM mappings
	•	framework lifecycle hooks

⸻

Cross-Cutting Concerns

Behavior applied across the system through framework features.

Examples:
	•	authentication
	•	logging
	•	caching
	•	transactions
	•	monitoring
	•	rate limiting

⸻

