Database Design

The semantic index should be stored in a database optimized for graph queries.

Preferred options:
	•	graph database (Neo4j)
	•	document store
	•	relational DB with graph structure
	•	vector index for semantic search

Key indexed entities:
	•	symbol
	•	file
	•	method
	•	class
	•	dependency
	•	annotation
	•	vulnerability pattern
	•	historical review signal

⸻

Nightly Indexing Pipeline

The indexing engine must run nightly or on schedule.

Steps:
	1.	Pull latest repository versions
	2.	Parse all repositories
	3.	Build AST (Abstract Syntax Trees)
	4.	Extract symbols
	5.	map dependency relationships
	6.	detect annotations
	7.	identify framework behaviors
	8.	detect security patterns
	9.	update dependency graph
	10.	store semantic index

⸻

PR Review Workflow

When a pull request arrives:
	1.	Detect changed files
	2.	retrieve indexed dependency graph
	3.	perform delta analysis
	4.	analyze only impacted dependency nodes
	5.	compare against indexed baseline
	6.	detect new vulnerabilities or logic issues

⸻

Critical Review Logic

When reviewing PR changes, the engine must follow these rules:

Rule 1

If a detected issue is already handled through a known dependency or framework mechanism, do not flag it.

Example:

If validation is handled by an annotation or middleware already indexed.

⸻

Rule 2

If a dependency relationship itself changes, trigger a deeper analysis.

Examples:
	•	security annotation removed
	•	database query modified
	•	validation layer bypassed
	•	transaction boundary changed

⸻

Rule 3

Known vulnerabilities already existing in the legacy codebase should not block PRs unless the change introduces a new vulnerability.

The system must enforce a “no new vulnerabilities” policy.

⸻

Rule 4

Prior review decisions should influence current reviews.

If reviewers historically approved a pattern, reduce its severity.

⸻

AI Analysis Requirements

AI should be used only for:
	•	semantic reasoning
	•	vulnerability detection
	•	pattern classification
	•	complex code reasoning

All structural analysis should be performed using deterministic parsers.

⸻

Performance Goal

PR reviews must execute in seconds rather than minutes by leveraging the pre-indexed semantic repository graph.

